"""Atlas content for patch 6.0, MSQ #781 As the Heavens Burn to #805 You're Not Alone, and the cp-ew-6-0 milestone
(after the quest that closes the patch). Arc tag y. Data only (docs/atlas/era-modules.md is the contract).

Researched 2026-11-19 from the saved Console Games Wiki wikitext (lanes W15–W20); every locator is an exact substring of
a quest's Journal, Steps or main dialogue (stage directions inside cutscenes included). Spoiler rules this module follows:
  - no surnames ("Leveilleur", "Junius", "Garlond", "Hext", "Ul Namo", "viator Galvus") outside locators;
  - the patch's own name stays out of displayed text; the milestone quest is cited only by its title;
  - several names can't be Atlas entries because they are substrings of older text: "Amon" (in "Among"), "Garlemald",
    "The Forum" (so the Forum's entry is "The Forum of Sharlayan") and "Sir" (in "Sirius"); they appear in text only;
  - reveals follow Marques → Cid, each from the step whose page states it: Venat → Hydaelyn and Fandaniel → Hermes at
    #791 (the Aitiascope and the Mothercrystal), M-017 → Stigma-1 at #803;
  - the companions lost on Ultima Thule (#794–#805) are summoned back at #805, so their losses are told in their
    presentations, not as ended relationships.
"""

def P(frm, until, scope, name, summary, claims, aliases=()):
    return dict(frm=frm, until=until, scope=scope, name=name, aliases=list(aliases), summary=summary, claims=claims)

(Y781, Y782, Y783, Y784, Y785, Y786, Y787, Y788, Y789, Y790, Y791, Y792, Y793, Y794, Y795, Y796, Y797, Y798, Y799,
 Y800, Y801, Y802, Y803, Y804, Y805) = (f"cp-msq-{n}" for n in range(781, 806))
