DECISIONS = [
 "**Five arcs (y1–y5)** cover every step from #781 to cp-ew-6-0 without sharing steps; each is 4–7 steps long, the last ending on the milestone.",
 "**Names that can't be entries:** \"Amon\" (a substring of \"Among\" in older text), \"Garlemald\" (named in 75 older texts), \"The Forum\" (older 5.55 text starts sentences with it) and \"Sir\" (inside \"Pharos Sirius\") would fail the name-visibility lint. "
   "So Amon and Sir are told in text only (Amon on `char-fandaniel` and `char-hermes`, Sir on `char-stigma-1`), Garlemald has no location entry, and the Forum's entry is named \"The Forum of Sharlayan\" (`org-forum`). Likewise the Ea are \"The Ea of Ultima Thule\" (`org-ea`), since \"The Ea\" is inside \"The East Aldenard Trading Company\".",
 "**Reveals at #791:** the page has Amon confess he was Hermes and took Fandaniel's seat and memories, so `char-fandaniel` is `revealed-as` `char-hermes` and Hermes carries \"Fandaniel\" as an alias from #791. "
   "Hydaelyn recalls the question she posed you in Elpis, so `char-venat` is `revealed-as` `char-hydaelyn`, and Hydaelyn carries \"Venat\" from #791 (Y'shtola only hedges the link at #782).",
 "**Reveal at #803:** M-017 is part of Stigma-1's shared intelligence (`rel-m-017-revealed-as-stigma-1`).",
 "**Losses on Ultima Thule** (Thancred #794, Estinien #797, Y'shtola and Urianger #800, G'raha #803, the twins #805) are told in presentations, not ended relationships, because all of them are summoned back at #805.",
 "**Zenos at the milestone:** the Journal says he breathed his last after the duel; his record says so. His open relationships are left for the lead (see the report). Krile's bargain (M806f, M806o) is told in Krile's and Zenos's records rather than as an open `aids` edge for a man who has just died.",
 "**The Scions disband only in appearance** at the milestone, so no membership ends; `rel-scions-hq-rising-stones` stays open (Tataru keeps it as a secret base).",
 "**Varshahn** speaks of his father, Midgardsormr (#790), and of himself as a simulacrum (#792); this part does not name whose simulacrum, leaving that link to the era that reveals it (#709b).",
 "**Left out as entities:** Theopauldin, Coph-coodg and the other Ea, Cookingway, Singingway, Growingway, Sleepingway, Barnier, Ojika, Jebke, Nidhana, the Bereaved Dragon, the Omicron units other than M-017, and the speaker in Elpis at the milestone's end.",
 "**Surnames out:** the twins' family name, Lucia's, Cid's, Nanamo's and Zenos's appear only in locators.",
]

